{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412371","formula":"COS","hill":"COS","elements":["C","O","S"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"O":1.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Carbonyl sulfide","ru":"Карбонилсульфид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Carbonyl sulfide is the chemical compound with the linear formula O=C=S. It is a colorless flammable gas with an unpleasant odor. It is a linear molecule consisting of a carbonyl double bonded to a sulfur atom. Carbonyl sulfide can be considered to be intermediate between carbon dioxide and carbon disulfide, both of which are valence isoelectronic with it.","ru":"Карбонѝлсульфи́д (оксид-сульфид углерода(IV)) — химическое соединение, смешанный оксид-сульфид углерода с формулой COS {\\displaystyle {\\ce {COS}}} . Структура молекулы линейна, аналогична структуре CO 2 {\\displaystyle {\\ce {CO2}}} и CS 2 , {\\displaystyle {\\ce {CS2,}}} при этом все три молекулы изоэлектронны друг другу. Карбонилсульфид можно считать промежуточным соединением между диоксидом углерода и сероуглеродом."},"fame":34,"pubchemCid":10039,"mass":60.08,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=O)=S","inchikey":"JJWKPURADFRFRB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"sulfanylidenemethanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10039","atoms":3,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.452,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"S"},{"x":1.314,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":0.138,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"}],"bonds":[[0,2,2],[1,2,2]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q412371","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbonyl_sulfide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%81%D1%83%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%84%D0%B8%D0%